==English==

===Etymology===
[[circa#English|Circa]] 1550, from circa 1500 {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|monologue|lang=frm}}, modeled on {{term|dialogue|lang=frm}}, ultimately from {{etyl|grc|en}} or via {{etyl|gkm|en}} {{term|μονόλογος||tr=monologos|lang=gkm|speaking alone|sc=Grek}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[monolog]] {{qualifier|US|noun}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|drama|lang=en}} A type of [[art]] that consist of [[soliloquy]], a long [[speech]] by one person.
# {{context|comedy|lang=en}} A long series of [[comic]] [[story|stories]] and [[joke]]s as an [[entertainment]].
# A long, uninterrupted utterance that monopolizes a conversation.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|drama}} [[soliloquy]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|a monopolizing utterance}} [[dialogue]]

